6. Full Instrument Specification
6.1 Instrument Schema
The instrument schema defines the structure of an instrument deposit.

It has the following fields:

instrument_id. A string. Required.

instrument_name. A string. Required.

description. A string. Required.

instrument_type. A string. Required. Examples: telescope, spectrometer, particle_detector, survey_questionnaire, sequencing_machine, thermometer, economic_index, other.

field. A string. Required.

subfield. A string. Optional.

manufacturer. A string. Optional.

model. A string. Optional.

serial_number. A string. Optional.

date_of_manufacture. A string in ISO8601 format. Optional.

date_of_first_use. A string in ISO8601 format. Optional.

operational_range. An object. It contains lower, upper, and units.

resolution. An object. It contains value and units.

precision. An object. It contains value and units.

accuracy. An object. It contains value and units.

uncertainties. An array of uncertainty objects.

measurement_kernel. An object. It contains type, parameters, and description.

selection_function. An object. It contains type, parameters, and description.

calibration_history. An array of calibration objects.

known_biases. An array of bias objects.

provenance. An object. It contains source, tool_version, and notes.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

numerical_verification_result. An object. Optional.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

dataset_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each uncertainty object has:

uncertainty_id. A string.

uncertainty_type. An enum. The values are statistical, systematic, calibration, environmental, other.

description. A string.

magnitude. An object. It contains value and units.

source. A string.

Each calibration object has:

calibration_id. A string.

calibration_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

calibration_source. A string.

calibration_reference. A string.

correction. An object. It contains value and units.

calibration_notes. A string. Optional.

Each bias object has:

bias_id. A string.

bias_description. A string.

bias_magnitude. An object. It contains value and units.

bias_range. An object. It contains lower and upper.

bias_source. A string.

bias_correction. An object. Optional. It contains value and units.

bias_notes. A string. Optional.

