7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Instrument
function createInstrument(instrument, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the instrument against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the STAG annotation is present, validate it.

Step 4. If the verification result is present, validate it.

Step 5. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. If the dataset reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 7. Generate an instrument ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 8. Insert the instrument.

Step 9. Insert the uncertainties, the calibrations, and the biases.

Step 10. Insert the STAG link, the verification link, the work link, and the dataset link if present.

Step 11. Insert the provenance.

Step 12. Insert the moderation record.

Step 13. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 14. Return the instrument_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Instrument
function readInstrument(instrumentId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the instrument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the uncertainties, the calibrations, the biases, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Instrument
function updateInstrument(instrumentId, instrument, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing instrument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new instrument.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the instrument_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Instrument
function deleteInstrument(instrumentId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing instrument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the instrument_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Instruments
function queryInstruments(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching instruments.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the instruments, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Instruments
function aggregateInstruments(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching instruments.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the instruments and the count.

7.8 Export Instrument
function exportInstrument(instrumentId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each instrument, call createInstrument.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching instruments.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per instrument. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Instrument
function moderateInstrument(instrumentId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing instrument. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the instrument_id and the status.

7.12 Instrument Comparison View
function instrumentComparisonView(instrumentIds, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read each instrument.

Step 3. Build the comparison by overlaying the measurement kernels and the selection functions on the same axes.

Step 4. Return the comparison.

7.13 Calibration Timeline
